      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I think that text chat should be targeted. That is, text messages should be addressed to a specific person. Circles with text, that pop up above your head, will clutter the space. Instead of a virtual tablet, simply display the screen where you can enter text either through the virtual keyboard or through voice input. Electronic translator also should be added, for example, Google-translate, since the problem of the language barrier is very relevant. Our interlocutor must also open a text screen to see the messages that we send to him. If its text screen is not opened, a notification appears when a new message arrives. If the message is in a foreign language, he can select the translation language in the built-in translator.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
